The attached image demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles enhance the uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a series of dot plots, shows that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or Nano-11 alone leads to moderate uptake, combining Nano-11 with OVA (Nano-11+OVA) results in significantly increased intracellular detection of both components within BMDCs. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantitatively confirms this, showing a substantial shift to higher fluorescence intensity for Nano-11+OVA-treated cells compared to OVA-only or other controls, indicating enhanced antigen delivery to BMDCs. This supports Nano-11's role as an effective vaccine delivery vehicle.